# Ashling, Rekindled. Turn 1: "whenever this creature enters ..., you may discard a card. If you do, draw a card" -
# Lightning Bolt is discarded and Brainstorm drawn. Turn 3: "at the beginning of your first main phase, you may pay {U}.
# If you do, transform Ashling" - Mox Sapphire pays it as the ability resolves, and Ashling turns over (CR 701.27a).
# Ashling, Rimebound's "whenever this creature transforms into Ashling, Rimebound ..., add two mana of any one color"
# triggers on the transform (CR 701.27e) and adds {B}{B} that pays only for spells with mana value 4 or greater
# (CR 106.6). Rimebound's own "at the beginning of your first main phase" abilities were not there as the phase began,
# so they did not trigger. The mana stays through the main phase and is gone at the beginning of combat (CR 106.4).
# Ashling is the same object (CR 701.27a): no summoning sickness again, and a 1/3 legendary Elemental Wizard now.

